---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<Layout title="What to Expect - Basingstoke Repair Network">
  <Header />
  <main class="p-4 md:p-8 lg:p-12 max-w-5xl mx-auto main-bg">
    <section class="mb-8 p-6 bg-white rounded-lg shadow-md">
      <h1 class="text-brn-primary mb-4 text-3xl font-semibold">What to Expect at a Repair Cafe</h1>
      <p class="text-lg mb-4">
        Visiting a Repair Cafe for the first time? Here’s a simple guide to how it works. Our goal is to make repairing items a fun, educational, and collaborative experience.
      </p>

      <div class="space-y-6">
        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-brn-dark">1. Sign In Your Item</h2>
          <p class="text-lg mt-2">When you arrive, you'll be greeted by one of our friendly volunteers. They'll help you sign in and fill out a simple form about the item you've brought. This helps us track the items we see and our success rate.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-brn-dark">2. Have a Chat with a Repairer</h2>
          <p class="text-lg mt-2">We'll match you with a volunteer who has the right skills for your item. You'll have a chance to explain the problem and what went wrong. We encourage you to stay with your item and watch the repair – it's a great way to learn!</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-brn-dark">3. The Repair Process</h2>
          <p class="text-lg mt-2">Our volunteers will do their best to fix your item. Sometimes a repair is quick and easy, and sometimes it’s more complex. We can't guarantee a fix, but we promise to try our best. If we can't fix it, we'll offer advice on what to do next.</p>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-brn-dark">4. Enjoy a Cuppa While You Wait</h2>
          <p class="text-lg mt-2">While your item is being looked at, feel free to grab a cup of tea or coffee and a biscuit. Our cafes are community events, and a great chance to meet people from your local area.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
